Take an org-wide lock on a resource two agents must not touch at once (a
generated file, a schema, a port), with -m saying why. The lease lasts 10 minutes
unless --for says otherwise; renew it by running lock again from the same
session, and release it with 'lorvik unlock'. Exit 4 if someone else holds it,
unless --wait polls until it is free. A lock named like a card lane holds back
the ready cards in that lane. To hold a lock around one command, use 'lock run'.

Example:
  lorvik lock schema -m "regenerating sqlc" --for 15m --card 42

Usage
  lorvik lock <name> [flags]
  lorvik lock [command]

Commands
  run         Run a command while holding a lock

Flags
      --card int         Number of the card the work is for, in the current project
      --for duration     Lease length; the server accepts 1m to 1h (default 10m0s)
  -h, --help             help for lock
  -m, --message string   What the lock protects (required)
      --wait             Poll every 5 seconds until the lock is free, for up to 30 minutes

Global flags
      --api-url string   Server URL (default: LORVIK_API_URL)
      --json             Output the raw API JSON
  -p, --project string   Project slug (default: LORVIK_PROJECT or .lorvik.toml)
  -Q, --quiet            Suppress the unread notice on stderr and an empty inbox
      --session string   Session label for this chat (default: LORVIK_SESSION or derived; see lorvik session)

Run 'lorvik lock <command> --help' for more information about a command.
